The position probe's first try failed through a launch mistake, not a model problem. I relaunched it correctly and started one more slot-reading cell. Nothing is decided yet.

**What went wrong**
- The identity check (job 193533) must give exactly the same answers as the original run before any shifted-position cell may start. It was meant to run 300 questions. It ran all 1,407 and hit its 50-minute limit at question 930, with no output file.
- Cause: the 300-row limit was passed as an environment variable. The eval script only reads it as its third command-line argument, so it ignored the value and ran every row.
- The scores it printed every 10 questions match the reference run at all 93 checkpoints (questions 10 to 930). That strongly suggests the check would pass, but the law asks for exact answer equality, so it still has to rerun.
- Its two dependent cells could never start, so I cancelled them.

**Running now**
| What | Rows | State |
|---|---|---|
| Identity check rerun, limit now given correctly (its log confirms 300 rows) | 300 | running, about 20 min |
| Positions moved to where a 40-page document puts them, seeds 42 and 43 | 1,407 each | start only if the identity check passes |
| Slot reading: keep the eighth of the `<MEM>` slots (compressed page tokens) the model attends to most, seed 42, 40 pages | 1,407 | 1,010 rows done, about 1 h left |
| Same slot-reading cell, seed 42, 10 pages | 1,407 | queued |

**One code change to know about**
- Another campaign (rebuild) committed a change to `pisco/model.py`. The padding fix the reference cells ran with is now opt-in and off by default.
- It cannot affect these page cells: each question's pages go through the compressor in one batch of many rows, and the fix only acts on one-row batches. The identity check proves this on 10-page documents.

**Budget**
- 93 of 96 cells used. The 3 left are exactly the plan: two seed-43 slot-reading cells and one second-judge re-score. Any further relaunch will need your approval.
- About 94 of 114 GPU-hours used, about 104 at the end.

**Next wake** starts when the identity check ends, at most 2 hours from now. It reads the result and launches the two seed-43 slot-reading cells.

I also clarified the row-limit rule in the campaign law, added the symptom to the known-issues table, and filed a tooling request so the job checker flags this mismatch.

Nothing needed from you.
